                        "form": "pétzouille"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a83a63c4-ab2e-3d76-a899-5bf23e7f5933",
                        "entry_id": "b195a565-929b-3d5c-9b12-6e9bc66331b4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Rustre, homme fruste, peu dégourdi. → voir péquenot, pignouf, plouc et rustaud"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0367637-9674-42d2-a6bb-ef67b73acbe0",
                                "sense_id": "a83a63c4-ab2e-3d76-a899-5bf23e7f5933",
                                "text": "Il l’appela tête de pioche, boîte à ragots, madame Pétesec, et s’emballa au point de traiter Coupeau lui-même de pedzouille, en l’accusant de ne pas savoir faire respecter un ami par sa femme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94b164fa-54c4-45fd-a3d1-ab2b7ed571a9",
                                "sense_id": "a83a63c4-ab2e-3d76-a899-5bf23e7f5933",
                                "text": "C'est très sain et très suffisant pour ce qu'on appelle un vulgaire pedzouille comme moi, reprit le duc ; on reste sur sa faim."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c3c3b3a-2332-4e1d-bea8-bdc5fc47174e",
                                "sense_id": "a83a63c4-ab2e-3d76-a899-5bf23e7f5933",
                                "text": "« F… moi le camp, eh purée, pedzouille ! F… moi le camp que j’t’ai assez vu."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dfeb187a-ad5b-4e47-b7c8-7cc9e479982a",
                                "sense_id": "a83a63c4-ab2e-3d76-a899-5bf23e7f5933",
                                "text": "« J’ai entendu l’élève Pégomas qui disait avec force : « Les demi-pensionnaires, c’est des pedzouilles ; et les boursiers, c’est des miteux : la preuve, c’est qu’on les fait manger au lycée, parce que chez eux, ils n’ont rien à bouffer. »"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c40cd57e-5dcf-4429-9b5f-8d39788af6c6",
                                "sense_id": "a83a63c4-ab2e-3d76-a899-5bf23e7f5933",
                                "text": "Nous ne sommes pas à cheval, nous, messieurs ; et fatiguer la bête n’est pas notre lot. Nous sommes des pedzouilles !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b68aa19e-7112-47dd-99d3-0f1349e40b0c",
                                "sense_id": "a83a63c4-ab2e-3d76-a899-5bf23e7f5933",
                                "text": "De quoi auraient-ils l’air, à cinq heures, dans les salons de la marquise de Fleurville ? D’un tas de pedzouilles bas-normands."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b80530c-9d0d-4b3e-a0c8-d452f65e74ec",
                                "sense_id": "a83a63c4-ab2e-3d76-a899-5bf23e7f5933",
                                "text": "Se faire traiter de pedzouille par un plouc pareil, c’est comique !"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "455f923e-ad52-406e-91b2-cd1e28c1592f",
                        "source_entry_id": "b195a565-929b-3d5c-9b12-6e9bc66331b4",
                        "source_sense_id": "a83a63c4-ab2e-3d76-a899-5bf23e7f5933",
                        "target_lang_word": "bumpkin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bumpkin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29ce43f3-ff29-315b-b01a-7019b3603ac7",
                                        "entry_id": "51995d9b-b3da-3f27-bef2-811c91c4156b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A clumsy, unsophisticated person; a yokel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed332c7c-b95c-3ba9-8b8a-0e94a3e098e8",
                                        "entry_id": "51995d9b-b3da-3f27-bef2-811c91c4156b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A short boom or spar used to extend a sail or secure a stay."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ae77b79-a5fd-3352-8187-129f08be7be5",
                                        "entry_id": "51995d9b-b3da-3f27-bef2-811c91c4156b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dance, a series of reels, Scottish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0e7008a-656d-48ee-839a-ec6bbfc96f2d",
                                                "sense_id": "1ae77b79-a5fd-3352-8187-129f08be7be5",
                                                "text": "They mix with Dancers, who now advance to the front, where a bumpkin, or dance of many interwoven reels, is performed; after which the Bride is led to a seat, and some of her Maidens sit by her."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "06d77ec6-23ac-4241-ab6a-d8662ee50cfb",
                        "source_entry_id": "b195a565-929b-3d5c-9b12-6e9bc66331b4",
                        "source_sense_id": "a83a63c4-ab2e-3d76-a899-5bf23e7f5933",
                        "target_lang_word": "yokel",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "yokel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd05ab03-c4f4-3337-971c-219e37bad38b",
                                        "entry_id": "6a64a1a4-8b6d-3f2d-8ce3-c65fef9652d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person from or living in the countryside, viewed as being unsophisticated or naive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "241ee8e0-5d79-48c2-928e-2588de644e27",
                                                "sense_id": "bd05ab03-c4f4-3337-971c-219e37bad38b",
                                                "text": "They love the scenery near their summer home, but have no desire to mix with the local yokels."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f059c18-1f33-4976-862b-494f98db9310",
                                                "sense_id": "bd05ab03-c4f4-3337-971c-219e37bad38b",
                                                "text": "“[…] my opinion at once is […] that this [robbery] wasn’t done by a yokel―eh, Duff?”\n“Certainly not,” replied Duff.\n“And, translating the word yokel, for the benefit of the ladies, I apprehend your meaning to be that this attempt was not made by a countryman?” said Mr. Losberne with a smile."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93d3e60a-dc1d-4fb9-8f90-f0ab634323c0",
                                                "sense_id": "bd05ab03-c4f4-3337-971c-219e37bad38b",
                                                "text": "[…] and yokels looking up at the tinselled dancers and poor old rouged tumblers, while the light-fingered folk are operating upon their pockets behind."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3aa769e0-87c8-4671-ba41-f01a0c459378",
                                                "sense_id": "bd05ab03-c4f4-3337-971c-219e37bad38b",
                                                "text": "He eyed the story-teller with unspeakable wonder. His mouth was agape in yokel fashion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64f3c5cf-b2a3-4105-a29c-5855f9bce9ec",
                                                "sense_id": "bd05ab03-c4f4-3337-971c-219e37bad38b",
                                                "text": "\"God damn and blast all you hamfisted yokels!\" he was saying. \"And you, sir, down there. Take that grin off your face and be more careful, or I'll have you clapped under hatches to sail with us today. Easy, there, easy! Christ, rum at seven guineas an anker isn't meant to be dropped like pig iron!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48e445bf-8265-4fa9-98f6-6671a8e8b99b",
                                                "sense_id": "bd05ab03-c4f4-3337-971c-219e37bad38b",
                                                "text": "I went to New York and bought myself a secondhand stretch limousine twenty-eight feet long, calculated to reduce the most blasé country-club sophisticates to bug-eyed yokels."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62179335-a3ef-4668-99ab-366fb63e72ea",
                                                "sense_id": "bd05ab03-c4f4-3337-971c-219e37bad38b",
                                                "text": "You may think that because you live in Brahmpur you have seen the world―or more of the world than we poor yokels see. But some of us yokels have also seen the world―and not just the world of Brahmpur, but of Bombay. […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bd7b1e2-0b32-412a-bed8-03006433c17a",
                                                "sense_id": "bd05ab03-c4f4-3337-971c-219e37bad38b",
                                                "text": "Some folk'll never eat a skunk, but then again some folk'll, like Cletus, the slack-jawed yokel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
